{
  "format": "bgsim.model",
  "language": "0.1.0",
  "name": "hydraulic-servo",
  "$comment": "Plan 9.6 (X2.5): a hydraulic position servo. The plant is a pure hydraulic/translation bond graph (D28): PressureSource 100 bar and Tank 1 bar feed the 4/3 valve subsystem (four VariableOrifice elements in a Wheatstone bridge; normalized area max(+-spool, 0) + 1e-4 with A = 1e-5 m^2, so the area is A_max*max(+-spool, 0) + 1e-9 m^2; Cd = 0.62, rho = 850 kg/m^3, p_tr = 1e5 Pa); the valve's A and B ports drive a HydraulicCylinder (piston 2e-3 m^2, annulus 1e-3 m^2, dead volumes 5e-5 m^3, bulk modulus 1.4e9 Pa) whose rod is a 1-junction with a 50 kg I, a 500 N*s/m R and a PositionSensor. The only non-bond-graph parts are the sensor (a kinematic integrator, D28 sensor exception), the 1 ms discrete PID clamped to +-1, and the two small inline glue blocks: ErrorSum (reference minus position; the stdlib Sum takes one vector input) and the valve's VDrive (splits the spool into the two normalized areas). The spool-to-area max is smoothed as 0.5*(u + sqrt(u^2 + 1e-12)) so the closed-centre spool does not sit on a non-smooth kink. PSensA/PSensB are pressure taps and pAmin/pBmin are check monitors. The cylinder starts at the valve's no-load equilibrium (pA = 33.667 bar, pB = 67.333 bar) with the PID integrator preloaded at the matching spool trim, because starting at the tank pressure lets the closed-centre valve lose the 50 kg rod and chatter on the orifice sign switches (W206).",
